Description:
    Scaffolds the outbound transfer ledger: a migration and model for
    MixinTransfer (with the runtime state machine), perform and reconcile
    jobs under app/jobs/mixin_transfers, and a Solid Queue recurring
    schedule for reconciliation.

    Usage:

        transfer = MixinTransfer.create!(
          recipient_id: user_id,          # Mixin user id of the recipient
          asset_id: ASSET_ID,
          amount: '1.5',
          memo: 'payout',
          trace_id: SecureRandom.uuid     # idempotency: re-sends are deduped
        )

    The record is enqueued on create and ends `confirmed` (with its
    transaction hash), `failed` (definitive rejection), or `reconciling`
    (timeout — resolved by the recurring job).

Example:
    rails generate mixin_bot:transfers

    This will create:
        db/migrate/xxx_create_mixin_transfers.rb
        app/models/mixin_transfer.rb
        app/jobs/mixin_transfers/perform_job.rb
        app/jobs/mixin_transfers/reconcile_job.rb
        config/recurring.yml

    Run `rails db:migrate` afterwards. If config/recurring.yml already
    exists, add the reconcile entry manually:

        production:
          mixin_transfers_reconcile:
            class: MixinTransfers.ReconcileJob
            schedule: every 5 minutes
